# Like .gitignore, but for "docker build": anything listed here is kept OUT of
# the build context, so it can never end up inside the image.

# --- Safety: never bake data or trained models into the image ---------------
# These are mounted from the host at run time (Raasta B). The CSV is unlicensed
# and must not be redistributed inside an image; models belong outside the code.
data/
artifacts/

# --- Speed + size: things the image simply doesn't need ---------------------
.git/
.venv/
notebooks/
audit/
docs/
*.md
# ...but keep README.md: pyproject's `readme = "README.md"` means the build
# (hatchling, during `uv sync`) fails if it's missing from the context.
!README.md

# Python caches / test noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
